{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>פורע</b> — For one who learns discipline will crown it and conceal it, and one who distances himself from it — it is as if he uncovers it and leaves it disheveled, from <i>כי פרוע</i>. That is, one who rejects the discipline of the sages desires to put his soul to death; and one who hears rebuke from their mouths acquires heart. And the meaning is knowledge and fear of HaShem."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:04.825252081Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}